  "spec_element": "requires",
  "proof_obligation": "initiation",
  "diagnosis": "The precondition of function contains is 'n <= (a.Length) + 1', which is off by one. It admits n = a.Length + 1, so the quantifier range 0 <= j < n includes j = a.Length. The access a[j] is then out of bounds. The counterexample shows this: with a.Length = 0 and n = 1, j = 0 is in range but a[0] does not exist. Because the precondition does not establish the facts needed for the body's array accesses to be well-formed, Dafny reports 'index out of range' at a[j]. Every caller (is_max) only passes n <= a.Length, so the bound can be tightened safely.",
  "repair": "requires n <= a.Length"
}
